      <!-- ===================== Benchmark ===================== -->
      <section class="bench" id="bench">
        <div class="bench-panel container vx-scanlines reveal">
          <div class="bench-head">
            <div>
              <p class="vx-kicker">// runner overhead · 3,270 tasks · 1,090 packages</p>
              <h2>Your tasks, plus a few percent.</h2>
            </div>
            <div class="bench-legend">
              <span class="legend"><span class="sw" style="background:var(--phosphor)"></span>vx</span>
              <span class="legend"
                ><span class="sw" style="background:var(--c-turbo)"></span>turborepo</span
              >
              <span class="legend"><span class="sw" style="background:var(--c-nx)"></span>nx</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="bench-rows">
            {
              benchRows.map((r) => {
                // Proportional within the row. The scale is the largest value that
                // is not an outlier (more than 10× the next largest); an outlier is
                // drawn clipped with a break so the others stay readable. No
                // minimum width — a small bar is small.
                const sorted = [...r.bars.map((b) => b.val)].sort((a, b) => b - a)
                const outlier = sorted.length > 1 && sorted[0]! > 10 * sorted[1]!
                const rowMax = (outlier ? sorted[1]! : sorted[0]!) * 1.05
                return (
                  <div class="bench-row">
                    <p class="task">{r.task}</p>
                    {r.bars.map((b) => {
                      const clipped = b.val > rowMax
                      const pct = clipped ? 100 : (b.val / rowMax) * 100
                      return (
                        <div
                          class={`bench-bar${b.best ? ' best' : ''}${b.name === 'baseline' ? ' baseline' : ''}${clipped ? ' clipped' : ''}`}
                          style={`--c:${b.c};--w:${pct}%`}
                        >
                          <span class="name">{b.name}</span>
                          <span class="track">
                            <span class="fill" />
                          </span>
                          <span class="disp">{b.disp}</span>
                          <span class="ratio">
                            {b.name === 'baseline' || b.best
                              ? ''
                              : `${(b.val / (r.bars.find((x) => x.best)?.val ?? 1)).toFixed(1)}×`}
                          </span>
                        </div>
                      )
                    })}
                  </div>
                )
              })
            }
          </div>
          <div class="bench-note">
            <p>
              Your tasks alone take 3m 38s on this graph — the ideal schedule, 10 perfectly parallel workers
              along the dependency graph. vx finishes the cold build in 3m 46s (+4%), Turborepo in
              5m 13s (+44%), Nx in 34m 44s (9.6× the schedule). Everything above the
              baseline is the runner.
            </p>
            <p>
              1,090 packages, 3,270 tasks, 100 dependency layers, identical commands, every runner
              pinned to the same concurrency, daemons on for the others, measured one at a time
              (2026-09-03, Turborepo 2.10.12, Nx 23.2.0, Apple silicon, 10 cores). The tasks are
              <code>sleep 1</code>, so the clock measures the runner and CPU measures its overhead:
              vx burned 35 s to build the whole graph cold, Turborepo 73 s, Nx 114 minutes. Warm,
              vx replays 3,270 tasks in 510ms; Turborepo 760ms; Nx 3.59s. Reproduce with
              <code>bun packages/vx-bench/compare.ts 100 11 1</code>; the committed results are this run. The dashed <em>baseline</em> is the theoretical best case: cold is the tasks' own 3m 38s on 10 perfectly parallel workers along the dependency graph, and a cached run, a restore and the CPU a runner burns are 0 in theory — every bar is the runner's overhead. Bars are proportional within a row; a bar more than ten times the next runner's is clipped with a break, and the numbers are exact.
            </p>
            <p>
              On a real Turbo monorepo — <code>solidjs/solid</code>, its own <code>turbo.json</code>, nothing
              rewritten — vx restores every output in 66 ms where Turbo takes 127 ms, replays a cached run in
              51 ms against 95 ms, and builds cold 12% faster; the same executed graph and the same 64
              files on both sides. The tables and the harness are in the
              <a href={href('benchmarks/')}>benchmarks</a>.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- ===================== Config ===================== -->
      <section class="config">
        <div class="config-grid container reveal">
          <div>
            <p class="vx-kicker">// configuration</p>
            <h2>Config is just<br />TypeScript.</h2>
            <p>
              Not JSON, not YAML. <code>vx.config.ts</code> is evaluated before hashing, so imports,
              shared presets and computed values all participate in the cache key. Tasks are shell
              commands; declare inputs and outputs with full type-safety.
            </p>
            <a class="btn btn-ghost" href={href('schema/')}
              >Read the config reference <span class="arr">→</span></a
            >
          </div>
          <div class="code-card">
            <div class="bar"><span class="dot"></span><span class="name">vx.config.ts</span></div>
            <pre><div><span class="tk-com">// vx.config.ts — next to any package.json</span></div><div><span class="tk-kw">import</span><span class="tk-txt"> {'{'} </span><span class="tk-fn">defineProject</span><span class="tk-txt"> {'}'} </span><span class="tk-kw">from</span><span class="tk-str"> '@vzn/vx'</span></div><div style="height:10px"></div><div><span class="tk-kw">export default</span><span class="tk-txt"> </span><span class="tk-fn">defineProject</span><span class="tk-punc">{'({'}</span></div><div><span class="tk-txt">  tasks: {'{'}</span></div><div><span class="tk-txt">    build: {'{'}</span></div><div><span class="tk-txt">      exec: {'{'} command: </span><span class="tk-str">'tsc -b'</span><span class="tk-txt"> {'}'},</span></div><div><span class="tk-txt">      dependsOn: [</span><span class="tk-str">'^build'</span><span class="tk-txt">],</span></div><div><span class="tk-txt">      cache: {'{'}</span></div><div><span class="tk-txt">        inputs: {'{'} files: [</span><span class="tk-str">'src/**'</span><span class="tk-txt">] {'}'},</span></div><div><span class="tk-txt">        outputs: {'{'} files: [</span><span class="tk-str">'dist/**'</span><span class="tk-txt">] {'}'},</span></div><div><span class="tk-txt">      {'}'},</span></div><div><span class="tk-txt">    {'}'},</span></div><div><span class="tk-txt">    test: {'{'}</span></div><div><span class="tk-txt">      exec: {'{'} command: </span><span class="tk-str">'bun test'</span><span class="tk-txt"> {'}'},</span></div><div><span class="tk-txt">      dependsOn: [</span><span class="tk-str">'build'</span><span class="tk-txt">],</span></div><div><span class="tk-txt">      cache: {'{'} inputs: {'{'} files: [</span><span class="tk-str">'src/**'</span><span class="tk-txt">] {'}'}, outputs: {'{'} files: [] {'}'} {'}'},</span></div><div><span class="tk-txt">    {'}'},</span></div><div><span class="tk-txt">  {'}'},</span></div><div><span class="tk-punc">{'})'}</span></div></pre>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- ===================== Migrate CTA ===================== -->
      <section class="migrate vx-grid-bg">
        <div class="glow"></div>
        <div class="beam" aria-hidden="true"></div>
        <div class="inner reveal">
          <p class="vx-kicker">// migrate</p>
          <h2>Warp in from Turbo or Nx.<br /><span class="phosphor">In an afternoon.</span></h2>
          <p>
            <code>bunx @vzn/vx-migrate</code> converts your <code class="turbo">turbo.json</code> or{' '}
            <code class="nx">Nx project graph</code> into a real <code>vx.config.ts</code>. The
            mapping is mechanical — keep your task graph and your speed, drop the daemon and the
            platform. What works there works here: the parity map names every behaviour a Turbo or
            Nx user relies on and the test that proves it.
          </p>
          <div class="row">
            <div class="cmd-pill"><span class="dollar">$</span> bunx @vzn/vx-migrate</div>
            <a class="btn btn-primary btn-lg" href={href('migrate/from-turborepo/')}
              >Read migration guide <span class="arr">→</span></a
            >
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- ===================== Footer ===================== -->
      <footer class="footer">
        <div class="foot-grid container">
          <div class="foot-brand">
            <div class="row">
              <img src={href('logo-mark.svg')} width="24" height="24" alt="vx" />
              <span class="word">vx</span>
            </div>
            <p>
              One task runner, built to be built on. One binary · MIT licensed.
            </p>
          </div>
          {
            Object.entries(footCols).map(([title, links]) => (
              <div class="foot-col">
                <p class="title">{title}</p>
                <div class="links">
                  {links.map((l) => (
                    <a href={l.h}>{l.t}</a>
                  ))}
                </div>
              </div>
            ))
